# FIXED DEFECT 2101, 2026-10-17, lane land215 (panel 216's compiler-engineer
# built the repair, alpha2 and the reader of a requirement over several lines).
#
# SYMPTOM: a constant the header spells `(__extension__ ({ 3; }))` stopped
# `heroes build` at exit 2, *internal error: compiling the generated C failed*,
# clang refusing a statement expression at file scope in the constant's own
# return-type assertion.
#
# CAUSE: a constant's type and constancy were asserted at file scope, where C
# has no statement expression; its accessor, a function, reads one.
#
# FIX: a constant of the program's own headers that its accessor returns is
# asserted inside that accessor (`emit/extern_assert.hero`'s
# `constant_assertions`, `emit/constant_accessor.hero`), so these build and
# print their value. The ones clang cannot fold are told, never exit 2:
# `tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2101-a-statement-expression-computed-when-read-is-told-not-constant.hero`.

extern "fixedbugs-2101-statement.h"
    constant ST_PURE: i32
    constant ST_TWO: i32

function main()
    print(ST_PURE)
    print(ST_TWO)
